IMPORT prelude
IMPORT types

-- Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ)
-- Part 3 Subpart 1 -- Functions and general powers of regulator (cll 20 to 23).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, 2026 No 339-1, retrieved 2026-09-11.
--
-- cl 4 defines the regulator as the chief executive of the Ministry -- the
-- department responsible for the administration of the Act. The subpart is
-- largely administrative, but three provisions state conditions an encoding can
-- decide: the cl 21(2) and 21(3) gate on an information notice, the cl 22(2)
-- confidentiality gate on sharing, and the cl 23(2) closed list of exceptions to
-- the disclosure prohibition.

§ `Part 3 Subpart 1 -- Functions and general powers of regulator`

§§ `20. Regulator's functions`

DECLARE `regulator function` IS ONE OF
    `section 20(1)(a) -- monitor and enforce compliance`
    `section 20(1)(b) -- co-operate and share information`
    `section 20(1)(c) -- promote education and awareness`
    `section 20(1)(d) -- publish guidance`
    `section 20(1)(e) -- advise the Minister on regulations`
    `section 20(1)(f) -- any other function conferred by legislation`

-- cl 20(2): the independence duty is scoped to cl 20(1)(a) and (b) only, and
-- runs against the Minister -- not against the department the regulator heads.
-- See NOTES.md, #13.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 20(2)
@export Decide whether the regulator must act independently of the Minister when performing a given function
GIVEN f IS A `regulator function` @desc Which of the six functions in cl 20(1) the regulator is performing.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator must act independently of the Minister` IF
        f EQUALS `section 20(1)(a) -- monitor and enforce compliance`
    OR  f EQUALS `section 20(1)(b) -- co-operate and share information`

§§ `21. Regulator's power to require information`

DECLARE `information notice` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 21(2)
    `the regulator considers the information necessary or desirable for its functions`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 21(3)(a) to (c)
    `the notice specifies the information that must be provided`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice specifies the date by which the information must be provided`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `onward disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states that disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 21(3)(c) is conditional: the statement is required only if the regulator
-- anticipates onward disclosure.
GIVEN n IS A `information notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 21(3)(c) statement requirement is met` IF
    IF   n's `onward disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`
    THEN n's `the notice states that disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`
    ELSE TRUE

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 21
@export Decide whether an information notice is validly issued under clause 21
GIVEN n IS A `information notice` @desc The notice: whether the regulator considers the information necessary or desirable for its functions, what the notice specifies, and whether onward disclosure under cl 22 is anticipated and stated.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information notice is validly issued` IF
        n's `the regulator considers the information necessary or desirable for its functions`
    AND n's `the notice specifies the information that must be provided`
    AND n's `the notice specifies the date by which the information must be provided`
    AND `the section 21(3)(c) statement requirement is met` n

§§ `22. Sharing information with law enforcement or regulatory agencies and overseas regulators`

DECLARE `information sharing` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 22(1)(a)
    `the regulator holds the information in relation to its functions under this Act`     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 22(1)(b)(i) and (ii)
    `the regulator considers it may assist a law enforcement or regulatory agency`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator considers it may assist an overseas regulator`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 22(2)
    `the regulator is satisfied appropriate confidentiality protections are in place`     IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 22
@export Decide whether the regulator may share information with an agency or overseas regulator
GIVEN s IS A `information sharing` @desc Whether the regulator holds the information in relation to its functions, whether it considers the information may assist the recipient, and whether it is satisfied that appropriate confidentiality protections are or will be in place.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator may share the information` IF
        s's `the regulator holds the information in relation to its functions under this Act`
    AND (    s's `the regulator considers it may assist a law enforcement or regulatory agency`
          OR s's `the regulator considers it may assist an overseas regulator` )
    AND s's `the regulator is satisfied appropriate confidentiality protections are in place`

§§ `23. Restriction on disclosure of information acquired under sections 21 and 22`

DECLARE `proposed disclosure` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `the person is the regulator or a person authorised by the regulator`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was acquired in exercising the section 21 or 22 powers`             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 23(2)(a) to (d)
    `the disclosure is for or in connection with the regulator's functions under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person to whom the information relates has consented`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is already in the public domain`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disclosure is required or permitted by this or any other legislation`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 23(2)(a) to (d) is a closed list of exceptions to the prohibition.
GIVEN d IS A `proposed disclosure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 23(2) exception applies` IF
        d's `the disclosure is for or in connection with the regulator's functions under this Act`
    OR  d's `the person to whom the information relates has consented`
    OR  d's `the information is already in the public domain`
    OR  d's `the disclosure is required or permitted by this or any other legislation`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 23
@export Decide whether an authorised person is prohibited from publishing or disclosing information
GIVEN d IS A `proposed disclosure` @desc Who proposes to disclose, whether the information was acquired under the cl 21 or 22 powers, and which of the four cl 23(2) exceptions is relied on.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is prohibited` IF
        d's `the person is the regulator or a person authorised by the regulator`
    AND d's `the information was acquired in exercising the section 21 or 22 powers`
    AND NOT `a section 23(2) exception applies` d

§§ `Scenario fixtures`

`a notice anticipating onward disclosure` MEANS `information notice` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "testing results, flagged for Police"
    `the regulator considers the information necessary or desirable for its functions`   IS TRUE
    `the notice specifies the information that must be provided`                          IS TRUE
    `the notice specifies the date by which the information must be provided`             IS TRUE
    `onward disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`                                   IS TRUE
    `the notice states that disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`                   IS FALSE

`a plain information notice` MEANS `information notice` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "routine account numbers request"
    `the regulator considers the information necessary or desirable for its functions`   IS TRUE
    `the notice specifies the information that must be provided`                          IS TRUE
    `the notice specifies the date by which the information must be provided`             IS TRUE
    `onward disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`                                   IS FALSE
    `the notice states that disclosure under section 22 is anticipated`                   IS FALSE

`a share to an overseas regulator without protections` MEANS `information sharing` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "overseas online safety regulator"
    `the regulator holds the information in relation to its functions under this Act`     IS TRUE
    `the regulator considers it may assist a law enforcement or regulatory agency`        IS FALSE
    `the regulator considers it may assist an overseas regulator`                         IS TRUE
    `the regulator is satisfied appropriate confidentiality protections are in place`     IS FALSE

§§ `Machine-evaluated cases`

-- cl 21(3)(c): a notice that anticipates onward disclosure but does not say so
-- fails, even though everything else about it is in order.
#EVAL `the information notice is validly issued` `a notice anticipating onward disclosure`
#ASSERT `the information notice is validly issued` `a notice anticipating onward disclosure` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the information notice is validly issued` `a plain information notice` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 22(2): the confidentiality gate is a precondition, not a consideration.
#ASSERT `the regulator may share the information` `a share to an overseas regulator without protections` EQUALS FALSE

-- cl 20(2): independence attaches to two of the six functions.
#ASSERT `the regulator must act independently of the Minister` `section 20(1)(a) -- monitor and enforce compliance` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulator must act independently of the Minister` `section 20(1)(b) -- co-operate and share information` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the regulator must act independently of the Minister` `section 20(1)(e) -- advise the Minister on regulations` EQUALS FALSE
